[COMMENTS]
STATION,Natural river section controlled by d/s gravel bar. Natural flow regime. GENERAL: A 40m wide river section. STATION HYDROMETRY: Natural river section controlled by d/s gravel bar at low flows and bridge arches at high flows. Flood Embankment on left bank at 4.5m. Multiple peak flow ratings applied across period of record, rated from gaugings and from 1990 ratings are extend using hydraulic model (which may also be applicable further back). FLOW RECORD: Records in early years are marred by substantial engineering works carried out on the bridge. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in April 2017 (WINFAP Files v5). FLOW REGIME: Natural to within 10% at Q95.
CATCHMENT,Impermeable Silurian formations, minor Boulder Clay and alluvium deposits. Catchment is mostly grassland/moorland, with extensive areas of forest. Patches of upland heath.
Qmed Suitability,Well gauged close to QMED. However, apply caution when using pre 1977 data as few gaugings to confirm ratings in early part of record.
Pooling Suitability,Flows upstream go out of bank, with potentially significant bypassing of the station.
[END]
